 "<0>Why decode cannot be parallelised across time:</0> token <1>t+{#}</1> depends on the sampled token <2>t</2> (<3>autoregressive loop</3>). The only parallelism left is across <4>requests</4> (<5>batching</5>) or via tricks like speculative decoding.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Latency</0>": "",
 "<0>Prefill</0> processes the whole prompt in one parallel pass (many tokens at once) and fills the KV cache. It is typically <1>compute-bound</1>.": "",
 "<0>Decode</0> generates one token per pass; each pass must stream all the weights from GPU memory, so it is typically <1>memory-bandwidth-bound</1>.": "",
 "That is why \"time to first token\" grows with prompt length while \"tokens per second\" is mostly about memory bandwidth.": "",
 "Rule of thumb: decode time per token ≳ weight bytes ÷ memory bandwidth ({#} GB ÷ {#} TB/s ≈ {#} ms at batch {#}).": "",
 "Prefill FLOPs ≈ {#} × parameters × prompt tokens. Decode does the same per token, but only for one token — too little work to keep the GPU busy.": "",
