 "▼ Dive in: <0>Lost in middle</0>": "",
 "The context window is the maximum number of tokens (prompt + generated reply) the model can attend to at once; the reference model's is {#}.": "",
 "Everything the model \"knows\" about your conversation must fit in the window; older text has to be truncated or summarised.": "",
 "Research suggests models often use information near the <0>start and end</0> of a long prompt better than information in the <1>middle</1> (\"lost in the middle\").": "",
 "Longer windows cost more: KV cache grows linearly, attention compute quadratically (<0>attention cost</0>).": "",
 "The U-shape is a hedged empirical finding (e.g. Liu et al. {#}) that varies by model; newer models and training recipes reduce it.": "",
 "Practical rule: put critical instructions at the start or end and retrieve only relevant chunks (<0>RAG</0>).": "",
